  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Tennessee's 5th Congressional District takes place in a dramatically redrawn district following a controversial mid-cycle redistricting in May 2026. The new map removed Davidson County (Nashville) and stretches from Williamson County north to the Kentucky state line and west to Shelby County, significantly altering the district's political composition. Incumbent Republican Rep. Andy Ogles faces a primary challenge from former Tennessee Agriculture Commissioner Charlie Hatcher, while a competitive Democratic primary features Columbia Mayor Chaz Molder, Memphis City Councilwoman Yolanda Cooper-Sutton, and several other candidates. Major election forecasters rate this seat as Solid/Safe Republican under the new map.",
